Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.76,0:00:08.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, good afternoon everyone.\N好的，大家下午好。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.24,0:00:12.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,How is everyone doing?\N大家都还好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.12,0:00:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have heard that this is the place to be.\N我听说这里就是最值得来的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.40,0:00:25.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Actually, this is uh AMD has been a long-standing supporter of OCP, but this is actually my first time at the OCP um Global Summit,\N呃，实际上，AMD一直是 OCP 的长期支持者，但这是我第一次参加 OCP 全球峰会，
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.79,0:00:30.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,and I have to say I'm just blown away by the scale of what uh we have here.\N我必须说，这里所展现的规模让我感到震撼。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.52,0:00:41.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I want to congratulate George and really the entire organizing committee for putting together just a fantastic event.\N所以，我要祝贺乔治以及整个组委会，成功打造了一场精彩绝伦的盛会。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.72,0:00:49.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, So, today what I'd like to do is maybe talk a little bit about what we see at AMD in terms of what's happening in the market.\N今天我想谈一谈，AMD 眼中当前市场正在发生的变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.62,0:00:54.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I can say for sure it's the fastest-moving market that I've ever seen.\N我可以肯定地说，这是我见过的变动最快的市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.54,0:00:59.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so much uh change, so much innovation, so much collaboration.\N这里有如此多的变化、创新和协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.56,0:01:04.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And maybe from an overarching standpoint, I would say, you know, for all of us at AMD,\N从整体来看，我想说，对我们 AMD 的所有人而言，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.68,0:01:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,we wake up every day thinking that our job is to really push the boundaries of high-performance\N每天醒来，我们都在思考如何真正推动高性能计算的边界，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.20,0:01:17.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,computing so that we can solve some of the most important challenges and problems in the world.\N以解决世界上一些最重要、最紧迫的挑战和问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.14,0:01:27.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to do this actually requires intense collaboration because I'm a big believer in there is no one company that has every answer to every solution.\N要做到这一点，实际上需要高度协作，因为我坚信没有任何一家公司能掌握所有解决方案的答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.72,0:01:35.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And frankly, the more we can bring the best of our companies together, the better we're going to do as an industry.\N诚实地讲，我们能把各家公司的优势汇聚得越多，整个行业就会表现得越好。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.23,0:01:39.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, AMD has opened as a foundation of our principles.\N因此，AMD 成为了我们原则的基石。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.24,0:01:42.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's one of the things that we think about when we develop technology.\N这是我们开发技术时会考虑的重要因素之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.43,0:01:45.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's one of the things that we think about when we develop our road map.\N这也是我们制定发展路线图时会考虑的重要因素之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.77,0:01:51.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look at the last 15 years of what OCP has really done,\N当你回顾过去15年OCP真正所做的事情，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.53,0:01:57.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's really been a huge part of our development road map going first going forward.\N它实际上已经成为我们发展路线图中至关重要的一环，推动我们不断前进。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.64,0:02:05.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,First on our open server platforms, from our very first platform that we did with Naples back in 2017,\N首先是我们的开放服务器平台，从2017年与合作伙伴微软共同打造的首个平台Naples开始，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.64,0:02:11.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,that was a very close collaboration with our partner Microsoft, but together we brought it to OCP.\N那是一次与微软的紧密合作，但最终我们共同将其提交给了OCP。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.41,0:02:20.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you look at, you know, over the last few years, a lot of work has come together on the networking side with the Ultra Ethernet Consortium,\N回顾近几年，在网络领域，大量工作汇聚到了超以太网联盟（\NUltra Ethernet Consortium）。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.16,0:02:23.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,with the work that we're doing around, you know, UALink and ESUN.\N包括我们在UALink和ESUN方面的努力。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.22,0:02:27.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of those are really important things for interoperability.\N所有这些都对互操作性至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.32,0:02:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm excited to talk about Helios.\N我很期待聊聊 Helios。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.04,0:02:38.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're going to talk a little bit about Helios today and the progress on that rack scale solution, which is again based on OCP standards.\N今天我们将简要讨论一下 Helios 以及该机架级解决方案的进展，它再次基于 OCP 标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.81,0:02:44.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then looking forward, I think we have lots more opportunities to collaborate together and these also become,\N展望未来，我认为我们有更多合作机会，这些机会也将成为，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.71,0:02:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,whether you're talking about MRC or Oak, these are also areas where there's just a tremendous opportunity for us to come together as an ecosystem.\N无论是讨论 MRC 还是 Oak，这些领域都为我们作为一个生态系统共同协作提供了巨大机遇。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.64,0:02:56.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with the notion of when we come together as an open ecosystem,\N当我们作为一个开放生态系统汇聚在一起时，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.63,0:03:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,we will actually accelerate the pace of innovation and get better solutions for our joint customers.\N我们实际上能加速创新步伐，为我们的共同客户带来更优的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.92,0:03:14.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, a little bit about the market, I think you guys know very well the AI market is truly transforming every part of the world,\N所以，简单谈谈市场，我认为你们非常清楚，AI 市场正在真正重塑世界的每一个角落，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.21,0:03:20.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,every industry that we're in, whether you're talking about healthcare or manufacturing or science.\N我们所处的每一个行业，无论是医疗健康、制造还是科学领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.25,0:03:23.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're seeing much, much more capability come across.\N我们正看到能力大幅提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.97,0:03:28.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like to say that we're in a world where computing equates to intelligence.\N我喜欢说，我们正处在一个计算即智能的世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.93,0:03:34.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you have the chance to be more intelligent, why wouldn't you try to get more capability?\N如果你有机会变得更智能，为什么不尝试获取更多能力呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.94,0:03:39.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's really what we're trying to do in terms of bringing all of that into the ecosystem.\N这正是我们努力将所有这些能力融入生态系统的核心目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.01,0:03:50.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just a few of the demand numbers that you see, every time I look at these charts, they tend to keep going up into the right.\N而且你看到的这些需求数据中，每次我查看这些图表时，它们总是持续向右攀升。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.28,0:03:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And people are always asking, well, you know, are we sure that we're doing productive work with all of the AI compute that we're putting on board?\N人们总在问，我们真的确定，我们投入的这些 AI 算力都在做有成效的工作吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.81,0:03:59.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the answer is absolutely yes.\N答案是绝对的，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.94,0:04:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we are doing a tremendous amount of work.\N我们正在做大量的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.04,0:04:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're getting more and more productive each time.\N我们每次都在变得越来越高效。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.04,0:04:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you kind of look at some of these demand numbers and you see like a 95 x increase in tokens per month over the past 2 years.\N是的，你看看这些需求数据，过去两年里，每月词元数量增长了 95 倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.60,0:04:20.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're now at some number like almost 40 quadrillion inference tokens a month.\N我们现在每月的推理词元数已接近 40 万亿。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.50,0:04:26.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um when you think about what that means in terms of useful AI, we get a lot of different data,\N当你思考这些数字对实际 AI 应用的意义时，我们获得了大量不同的数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.91,0:04:34.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I think the data that's most important to me is what do I see when I talk to customers and when I spend time with the largest users.\N但对我来说最重要的数据是，当我与客户交流，与最大用户群体共处时，我看到了什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.11,0:04:35.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know,\N你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.11,0:04:40.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,clearly training continues to be extremely important and we're going to continue to need the largest\N显然训练仍然极其重要，我们仍需要全球最大的
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.18,0:04:44.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,training clusters in the world and we're going to continue to push the envelope on capability.\N训练集群，并且我们仍将持续推动能力的边界。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.93,0:04:51.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's call it, you know, 5 x increase every year since 2020 and that doesn't look like that's going to change.\N我们可以把它称为，自2020年以来每年增长5倍，而且这种情况似乎不会改变。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.99,0:04:54.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's going to continue going on.\N这种趋势将持续下去。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.10,0:05:01.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but we've always thought that where AI really pays off is when inference overtakes training.\N嗯，但我们一直认为，AI真正产生效益的时刻，是推理超过训练的时候。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.86,0:05:11.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look at the numbers over the last few years, especially this year in 2026, this year is really the year of inference.\N当你回顾过去几年的数据，尤其是2026年这一年，这一年确实是推理的爆发之年。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.25,0:05:18.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the year where we believe inference is now about 60% of the market going forward.\N这一年，我们认为推理将占市场总量的约60%，并且这一趋势将持续下去。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.60,0:05:25.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's not just inference, it's really the agentic workloads that have really taken off.\N而且不仅仅是推理，真正爆发的是代理式工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.20,0:05:27.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you look at some of these numbers.\N所以你来看一下这些数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.54,0:05:33.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is some new data from Open Router which routes requests across many models\N这是来自 Open Router 的最新数据，它会将请求路由到多个模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.40,0:05:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,and what you see is that the amount of human traffic has gone up steadily,\N你看到的是人类流量稳步上升，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.40,0:05:44.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,but what's really grown is the amount of agentic traffic and we're seeing a 14\N但真正大幅增长的是代理式流量，我们今年看到代理式流量增长了14倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.79,0:05:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,x growth just this year in the amount of agentic traffic that is going through.\N这种增长趋势清楚地说明了AI工作的强大潜力。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.48,0:05:54.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that kind of tells you the power of the of AI working.\N这种趋势清楚地说明了AI工作的强大潜力。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.03,0:05:57.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is we're training better models.\N我们正在训练更优秀的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.72,0:06:03.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We now have the opportunity not just to do inference, but we have the opportunity to solve problems.\N我们现在不仅有机会进行推理，更有机会解决实际问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.31,0:06:12.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with that we're seeing a lot more opportunity for growth and you know, really productive growth going forward.\N这样一来，我们看到了更多增长机会，未来将实现真正富有成效的增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.52,0:06:19.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, George showed some numbers about the TAM as it relates to the infrastructure.\N现在，乔治展示了一些与基础设施相关的总可寻址市场数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.06,0:06:28.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is some information on the the TAM as it relates to the silicon and the systems which the silicon the core which is what you know,\N这是关于市场规模与硅片及硅片所构成系统之间关系的一些信息，其中核心部分就是你所了解的。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.36,0:06:29.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're focused on.\N我们关注的。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.72,0:06:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're seeing a couple things, right?\N我们看到了几件事情，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.20,0:06:40.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,First of all, we're seeing the data center AI accelerator TAM grow to close to 1 and 1/2 trillion by the time we get to 2030,\N首先，我们看到数据中心AI加速器的市场规模到2030年将接近1.5万亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.64,0:06:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is a fantastically large number.\N这是一个极其庞大的数字。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.92,0:06:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why there's so much excitement and innovation in this area.\N这就是为什么这一领域充满如此多的激动与创新。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.64,0:06:57.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we've also seen that with agentic workloads, we've seen a very significant increase in what was known as the traditional CPU TAM.\N但我们还看到，随着代理式工作负载的出现，传统CPU的市场规模出现了显著增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.44,0:07:03.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you were to look at this number, you know, let's call it even a year ago, you know, people would have said, "Hey,\N如果你现在回头看这个数字，哪怕是去年，人们可能会说：“嘿，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.57,0:07:11.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,the CPU market is probably a 20 billion-dollar market growing you know, single digits over the next few years."\NCPU 市场可能是一个规模约 200 亿美元的市场，未来几年将保持个位数增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.46,0:07:23.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have actually raised the TAM on this three times in the last nine months because we've seen that much growth in the overall CPU demand,\N我们在过去九个月里已经三次上调了这个市场的总可寻址市场规模，\N因为我们看到了整体 CPU 需求的显著增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.43,0:07:29.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,which we now believe will grow at approximately 50% CAGR over the next four or\N我们现在认为，未来四到五年内，该市场规模将大约以 50% 的年复合增长率增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.57,0:07:34.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,five years to over a 200 billion-dollar TAM by the time you get to 2030.\N到 2030 年，总可寻址市场规模将超过 2000 亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.58,0:07:39.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that has implications on how you want to build systems.\N这对系统构建方式有着重要影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.68,0:07:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The fact is, you know, there's no one size fits all when it comes to compute.\N事实是，计算领域没有放之四海而皆准的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.88,0:07:54.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You actually need the right compute for the right workload, and that's across CPUs and GPUs and ASICs and FPGAs and all of the mix in between.\N你实际上需要为特定工作负载选择合适的计算资源，\N这涵盖了 CPU、GPU、ASIC、FPGA 以及它们之间的各种组合。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.88,0:07:59.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's the foundation of how we have, you know, really focused at AMD.\N这正是我们专注于 AMD 的基础。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.96,0:08:07.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when you think about, you know, the three things that we think are most important, um the first and foremost is we're a compute company.\N所以，当你思考我们认为最重要的三件事时，首要的是我们是一家计算公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.90,0:08:09.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compute equals intelligence.\N计算即智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.38,0:08:11.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need to have compute leadership.\N我们必须保持计算领域的领导地位。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.26,0:08:18.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that compute leadership is across, um every aspect of that, you know, CPU, GPU,\N这种计算领导地位涵盖所有方面，包括 CPU 和 GPU 等。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.15,0:08:23.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,ASIC, all of those capabilities because we need the right compute for each application.\NASIC，所有这些功能，因为我们需要为每个应用提供合适的计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.64,0:08:26.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we also believe that you're going to see AI everywhere.\N嗯，我们还认为，你会看到AI无处不在。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.92,0:08:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're going to spend a lot of time over the next few days probably talking about the big iron, um in the cloud, hyperscale, and enterprise.\N所以，接下来几天我们很可能会花大量时间讨论云中的大型设备、超大规模和企业级系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.64,0:08:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're big believer in the fact that you're going to see AI infused through every aspect of the edge as well as the client in the ecosystem.\N我们坚信，AI将渗透到边缘和生态系统中客户端的方方面面。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.48,0:08:53.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the more that we can get the standards across those, uh those different form factors to be the same, the more that we can get the software,\N我们越能让这些不同形态的设备在标准上保持一致，就越能实现软件在所有系统间的通用。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.21,0:09:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh to work across all of those systems, the better off we're going to be to provide productivity to the end users of, um these systems.\N这样我们就能更好地为这些系统的最终用户提升生产力。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.84,0:09:07.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the middle point is the point that's most relevant for today.\N而中间这一点，正是今天最相关的。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.96,0:09:11.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Open is a foundation of what we do at AMD.\N开放是我们AMD一切工作的基础。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.96,0:09:19.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are big, big believers, as I said, in the idea that open platforms enable collaboration.\N正如我所说，我们坚信开放平台能促进协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.65,0:09:26.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Collaboration enables the best of each company to bring to the table so that we have better overall solutions.\N协作能让每家公司最优秀的能力汇聚在一起，从而带来更优的整体解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.95,0:09:31.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the fact is, you know, AI at scale is a team sport.\N事实是，大规模AI是一场团队运动。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.26,0:09:37.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is a an area where we want to bring, uh the the of the industry, uh together.\N这正是我们希望将整个行业凝聚在一起的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.79,0:09:46.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'll talk a little bit today about the work that we're doing on rack-scale innovation because it's uh been a very, very exciting uh year for us.\N今天，我想简单聊一下我们在机架级创新方面的工作，因为对我们来说，这一年非常非常令人振奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.02,0:09:52.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then a little bit about what we see going forward in terms of the agentic infrastructure.\N另外，关于我们在代理式基础设施方面所看到的未来趋势。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.72,0:09:57.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you know, first and foremost, I think all all of you guys know this, but you know,\N所以啊，你们都知道，这一点最重要，你们都明白的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.69,0:10:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,this has been a principle um frontier AI has higher and higher demands on what all of us do.\N这一直是一个原则，前沿人工智能对我们的各项工作提出了越来越高的要求。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.92,0:10:15.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, our job is to bring a solution to the market that allows our end users to use the technology as fast as possible,\N我们的工作是尽快将解决方案推向市场，让终端用户能以最快速度使用这项技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.45,0:10:24.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,as efficiently as possible, with as little friction as possible to get the best tokens for dollar, to get the best tokens for outcome.\N尽可能高效地，尽可能减少摩擦，以获得每美元和每结果的最佳词元。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.64,0:10:26.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to do that, you need all of these pieces.\N要做到这一点，你需要所有这些组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.04,0:10:28.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to have leadership compute.\N你需要具备领导力算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.02,0:10:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to have an open rack architecture.\N你需要采用开放的机架架构。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.20,0:10:37.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to have um a fabric that allows you to scale uh across um the uh systems.\N你需要一种能够让你在各个系统间实现扩展的织物。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.68,0:10:44.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we also need to care about things like efficiency and serviceability, um as well as, you know, overall turnkey solutions.\N我们还需要关注效率和可维护性，以及整体的交钥匙解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.89,0:10:46.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you need all of these things.\N所以，你需要所有这些。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.99,0:10:55.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I have to say um all of these things were critical when we decided to uh bring out the Helios uh architecture.\N我必须说，当我们决定推出 Helios 架构时，所有这些因素都至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.00,0:11:00.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We launched Helios in July of this year, just a couple of months ago.\N我们在今年七月推出了 Helios，也就是几个月前的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.40,0:11:07.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I will say, you know, our view is that this is the highest performance AI rack in the industry.\N我想说的是，我们认为这是业界性能最高的 AI 机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.64,0:11:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,72 GPUs working together as a single accelerator.\N72 块 GPU 协同工作，作为一个单一加速器。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.76,0:11:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,More than 18,000 GPU compute units.\N超过 18,000 个 GPU 计算单元。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.96,0:11:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,4,600 Zen 6 cores.\N4,600 个 Zen 6 核心。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.00,0:11:24.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each compute tray is just a little bit heavy um at uh 160 lb.\N每个计算托盘重量略重，大约 160 磅。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.84,0:11:28.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the total rack is nearly 7,000 lb.\N整个机架的重量接近 7,000 磅。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.32,0:11:33.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um it's a little bit of a machine.\N所以，这确实是一台相当庞大的机器。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.40,0:11:41.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think George said something like everyone gets a little wider as the years pass.\N我觉得乔治说过类似的话：随着年岁增长，每个人都会变得稍微宽一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.92,0:11:44.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I don't want to say that about our racks,\N我不想用这话来形容我们的机架，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.49,0:11:56.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I would say we made a very deliberate choice with Helios uh to use the um OCP um open rack wide standard.\N但我想说的是，我们在设计 Helios 时，明确选择了 OCP 开放机架宽标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.09,0:12:03.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it is uh one of the most ambitious engineering feats that I've ever had a chance to be part of in my career.\N呃，这是我职业生涯中参与过的最具雄心的工程壮举之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.45,0:12:06.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this was co-engineered with Meta, um our partner.\N呃，这是与我们的合作伙伴 Meta 联合设计的。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.32,0:12:09.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know you're going to hear from Santosh a little bit later on.\N我知道你稍后会听到桑托什的分享。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.30,0:12:12.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I have to say it has been a tremendous partnership.\N呃，我必须说，这是一次非常出色的合作伙伴关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.81,0:12:18.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know, we started with the notion of look, there going to be a lot of accelerators out there.\N而且你知道，我们一开始的想法是，市场上将会有大量加速器。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.41,0:12:20.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it is not one-size-fits-all.\N呃，这并不是万能的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.64,0:12:23.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not you know, one company has all the best parts.\N并不是说某一家公司拥有所有最好的部件。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.00,0:12:29.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we want to do is make it really easy for a heterogeneous data center environment.\N我们希望让异构数据中心环境的使用变得非常简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.75,0:12:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cuz there's a firm belief in that you're going to need a mix of CPUs, GPUs, uh purpose-built ASICs.\N因为大家坚信，你将需要 CPU、GPU 以及专为特定用途设计的 ASIC 的组合。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.36,0:12:41.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're going to want to be in a similar data center environment.\N它们都将希望运行在类似的数据中心环境中。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.26,0:12:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're not going to want to switch out every component every time you change an accelerator.\N你不会希望每次更换加速器时都更换所有组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.57,0:12:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're really going to try to to standardize as much as you can so that you are differentiating on the things that make the most difference.\N你真正要做的是尽可能实现标准化，以便在真正带来差异化的方面进行区分。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.40,0:13:00.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's exactly what we've done with um the Helios platform together with Meta.\N这正是我们与 Meta 一起所做的。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.34,0:13:06.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think what we see here is um a tremendous opportunity to bring the ecosystem together.\N我认为这里展现出了一个巨大的机会，可以将整个生态系统整合在一起。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.02,0:13:16.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, lots and lots of partners are needed to make Helios happen, but it includes um the uh open architecture on the rack standpoint,\N因此，要让 Helios 成功，需要大量合作伙伴，其中包括机架层面的开放架构，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.59,0:13:21.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,um open uh power shelves, open networking, and the overall management system.\N开放的电源机架、开放的网络连接，以及整体管理系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.99,0:13:26.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're very uh happy with how Helios uh uh has come along.\N我们对 Helios 目前的发展非常满意。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.50,0:13:31.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um as part of this, uh networking is a huge piece of this ecosystem.\N作为其中一部分，网络是这个生态系统中极为关键的一环。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.09,0:13:35.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would say that we've spent um quite a bit of time internally, you know, for us,\N我想说，我们内部投入了大量时间，尤其是负责数据中心解决方案的诺罗德，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.59,0:13:42.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh Norrod who runs the data center solutions for us, in terms of architecting this thing, um whole thing coming together.\N他一直在构思整个系统的架构，推动各项要素整合到位。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.31,0:13:46.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, our principle is we wanted to use the best solution that was available.\N但我们的原则是，要采用当时可用的最佳解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.18,0:13:52.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the best solution that would be was available would mean bringing in uh the leading networking partners in the world.\N而最佳解决方案意味着引入全球领先的网络合作伙伴。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.54,0:13:57.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're doing tremendous work with Broadcom, Cisco, Arista, HPE, DriveNets.\N我们正与博通、思科、阿瑞斯、惠普企业、DriveNets 开展卓有成效的合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.35,0:14:05.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the idea is to have leading front-end solution, um leading scale-up solution with uh UALink over Ethernet,\N目标是打造领先的前端解决方案，以及基于以太网的 UALink 的领先扩展解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.31,0:14:11.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,as well as ESUN, and then leading scale-out solutions, um as well, that are uh ahead of the industry.\N还有ESUN，以及领先的横向扩展解决方案，这些方案也领先于行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.43,0:14:16.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of this is delivered through the OCP open ecosystem.\N所有这些都通过OCP开放生态系统实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.08,0:14:21.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of this um openness extends to software, as well.\N所有这些开放性也延伸到了软件层面。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.12,0:14:32.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the idea of software is, you know, we need to make for that it's super easy for our customers to bring new workloads onto our accelerators.\N软件的理念是，我们需要让客户能够轻松地将新工作负载迁移到我们的加速器上。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.16,0:14:37.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to do that, you want to have, let's call it, the leading open communities running natively.\N为此，你需要拥有原生运行的领先开源社区。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.63,0:14:42.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have the top 15 open AI communities that are supporting AI AMD natively.\N我们拥有前15大支持AI AMD原生的开源社区。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.94,0:14:45.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have seen uh significant benefit.\N我们已经看到了显著的好处。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.63,0:14:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perhaps this is one of the largest benefits that we've seen of AI.\N这可能是我们所见到的AI带来的最大好处之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.72,0:14:58.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is a case where, you know, agentic AI can actually continue to make the performance of the hardware um better over time.\N在这个案例中，代理式AI实际上能够随着时间推移持续提升硬件性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.64,0:15:05.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh just to give you one uh statistic, um Hyperloom is our agentic AI solution,\N给你一个数据作为参考，Hyperloom是我们的代理式AI解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.48,0:15:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we've had it running continuously running for uh the Hugging Face models.\N我们已让其持续运行于Hugging Face模型上。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.44,0:15:20.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, over 14,000 models on Hugging Face with no humans in the loop, we've seen almost a 40% improvement in performance just having the agentic AI run.\N在Hugging Face上超过14,000个模型，全程无人干预，\N仅靠代理式AI运行，我们就看到了接近40%的性能提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.70,0:15:30.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the key is open ecosystems on hardware, software bringing the opportunity to get significant performance uh capability to our end users.\N因此，关键在于硬件和软件上的开放生态系统，这能为我们终端用户带来显著的性能和能力提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.76,0:15:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, if you take a look at all of those pieces, what does that mean to the end user?\N所以，如果你看看所有这些组件，这对终端用户意味着什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.44,0:15:42.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,The Helios rack delivers um the highest compute in the industry, the highest memory uh capacity,\NHelios 机架提供了业内最高的计算能力，最高的内存容量，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.33,0:15:49.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,the highest memory bandwidth, and the highest networking uh capacity or capability across um the industry.\N最高的内存带宽，以及业内最高的网络容量或能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.95,0:16:01.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to give you some idea of the numbers, uh we believe that uh we're translating into 30% more tokens per dollar using uh the Helios uh solution.\N为了让你对数据有个直观了解，我们认为，使用 Helios 解决方案，\N每美元可处理的词元数量能提升 30%。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.44,0:16:04.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, all the PowerPoint sounds great.\N现在，所有的幻灯片听起来都很棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.36,0:16:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's probably better to see a few pictures.\N也许看几张图片会更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.08,0:16:07.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,\N所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.41,0:16:08.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,um let me show\N让我来展示一下
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.66,0:16:09.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,you a\N给你看个
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.16,0:16:09.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,little\N小小的
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.75,0:16:10.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,bit\N一点
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.08,0:16:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,here.\N在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.52,0:16:50.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,People told me that rack-scale solutions would be the hardest thing that we've ever done.\N有人告诉我，机架级解决方案将是我们做过的最困难的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.10,0:16:52.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think they were absolutely right.\N嗯，我认为他们完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.85,0:17:01.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Helios is absolutely uh the most uh sophisticated and complex system that we have built um at AMD together with our partners.\N赫利俄斯绝对是我们在AMD与合作伙伴共同打造的最复杂、最精密的系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.29,0:17:05.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh but I'm very happy to say that Helios is in production today.\N但我很高兴地告诉大家，赫利俄斯现在已投入生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.28,0:17:08.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we started shipping production in September.\N我们从九月开始发货生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.36,0:17:16.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first systems are installed at our leading customers, OpenAI, Meta, Micro System uh Microsoft, um Oracle,\N首批系统已部署在我们的主要客户——OpenAI、Meta、\N微系统（Micro System）和微软、甲骨文，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.00,0:17:25.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anthropic, and we continue to see just tremendous learnings when we bring all of these these pieces together.\N以及Anthropic，当我们把这些组件整合在一起时，我们持续获得巨大的学习成果。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.79,0:17:31.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, our production will continue to ramp through the fourth quarter into the first half of next year, but what we did is,\N因此，我们的生产将持续在第四季度加速，并延续到明年上半年，但我们所做的，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.35,0:17:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, with the OCP standard working together with our partners was just fantastic engineering overall.\N与OCP标准合作，携手合作伙伴，整体工程表现非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.20,0:17:44.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm happy to say there's significant growing adoption of Helios, not only the largest model companies,\N很高兴地宣布，赫利俄斯的采用正在显著增长，不仅在大型模型公司中，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.69,0:17:50.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,but in addition a number of AI native companies, a number of the overall ecosystem ODMs, OEMs.\N而且在众多AI原生公司、整个生态系统中的ODM和OEM中也广泛采用。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.65,0:17:53.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know a bunch of you are in the audience today.\N我知道今天在座的各位中有不少人。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.67,0:17:55.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Neoclouds, thank you.\N新云厂商，谢谢你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.36,0:17:57.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for all of the collaboration on Helios.\N感谢大家在赫利俄斯项目上的协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.61,0:18:05.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to continue to broaden this going forward as we, you know, think about, you know, the next next few quarters.\N接下来我们会继续拓展这一领域，随着我们思考未来几个季度的发展方向。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.32,0:18:11.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, with that, maybe I'll transition a little bit to agentic infrastructure.\N那么，接下来我稍微转向一下，谈谈代理式基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.64,0:18:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I would say that this is probably the place where that has been the most activity over the last let's call it 6 months or so.\N我认为在过去大约六个月里，这里可能是活动最频繁的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.16,0:18:23.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's been a lot of talk about agents.\N关于智能体的讨论非常多。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.31,0:18:25.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would say the excitement is real.\N我认为这种热情是真实的。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.15,0:18:31.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we've all seen just tremendous productivity whether in personal use cases or\N我们所有人都看到了巨大的生产力提升，无论是个人使用场景还是企业使用场景，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.49,0:18:37.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the in enterprise use cases and it's moving much faster than we thought.\N而且进展速度远超我们的预期。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.43,0:18:41.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, kind of some of the examples out there that are pretty interesting.\N所以，目前有一些相当有趣的案例。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.28,0:18:49.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, Muse has kind of recaptured the imagination as to what AI can do for the consumer.\N例如，Muse 重新激发了人们对 AI 能为消费者带来什么的想象。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.09,0:18:54.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,This number of 5 million downloads of Meta Muse was as of the end of September.\N截至九月底，Meta Muse的下载量已达500万次。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.58,0:18:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that was like the first, you know, couple weeks.\N那大概就是最初的、你知道的那两三周。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.20,0:18:59.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sure Santosh will talk about it more.\N我相信桑托什会讲得更详细。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.28,0:19:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think I read this morning in the Wall Street Journal that they're down to now up to 9 million downloads of Meta Muse in just the first month or so.\N我今早在《华尔街日报》上看到，Meta Muse在第一个月左右的下载量已达到900万次。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.00,0:19:16.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, OpenAI has talked about using um, 10,000 agents to solve some of the most difficult math problems um,\N你知道，OpenAI曾提到使用大约1万个智能体来解决一些最困难的数学问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.88,0:19:20.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,in uh, history that haven't, you know, really seen the full uh, solution.\N这些问题在历史上从未真正得到过完整解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.77,0:19:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anthropic talks about using R&D agents to uh, really get a quad working.\NAnthropic提到使用研发智能体来真正让四核处理器运行起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.28,0:19:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these say that agentic usage is real.\N所有这些都说明，代理式应用是真实存在的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.28,0:19:37.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can tell you within AMD, we're actively using agents both on our silicon development as well as on our software development.\N我可以告诉你们，在AMD内部，我们正在积极使用智能体，既用于硅片开发，也用于软件开发。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.29,0:19:39.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,I gave you the example of Hyperloom.\N我举了Hyperloom的例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.03,0:19:47.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you say, "Okay, everyone talks about agents, but what do you actually need uh, for agents?"\N所以你会说：“好吧，大家都在谈智能体，但你实际上需要什么来支撑智能体？”
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.19,0:19:53.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think the most important thing to realize is that agents actually are not one thing.\N我认为最重要的一点是，智能体实际上并不是单一的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.70,0:19:57.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, agents, like people, there are lots of different types of agents.\N你知道，智能体和人一样，有各种不同类型。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.41,0:20:01.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need the right agents for the right um, application.\N你需要为特定的应用场景选择合适的智能体。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.32,0:20:04.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for that, you actually need the right compute.\N而要做到这一点，实际上你需要合适的计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.21,0:20:09.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when you're talking about personal agents, you probably want the densest agents possible.\N所以，当你谈论个人智能体时，你可能希望它们尽可能密集。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.64,0:20:14.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are simpler tasks, and you want them to be uh, you know, very efficient.\N这些任务更简单，你希望它们高效运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.67,0:20:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want them to be maximum number of agents per watt, so you are uh, saving your power correctly.\N你希望每瓦特功率能支持尽可能多的智能体，这样才能正确地节省电力。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.64,0:20:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, you know, that's one class of agents.\N这是一类智能体。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.96,0:20:28.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, you talk about enterprise agents, where you're doing a lot of different types of activities, and so you want them to be pretty balanced.\N当你谈到企业级智能体时，它们需要执行多种不同类型的活动，因此你希望它们性能均衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.08,0:20:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or you're talking about some of the hardest compute problems out there, these technical compute agents.\N或者你面对的是当前最复杂的计算难题，也就是技术型计算智能体。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.76,0:20:38.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going You're going to want them to be bleeding-edge performance, kind of the the best of the best.\N你希望它们具备最前沿的性能，达到顶尖水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.69,0:20:42.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, each of these agents needs a different type of compute.\N因此，每种智能体都需要不同类型的计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.54,0:20:48.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we believe is each of these agents also need the right type of rack.\N我们认为，每种智能体还需要合适的机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.11,0:20:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that means you're going to see a certain type of rack in hyperscale environments, where you might have disaggregated CPU and GPU racks.\N这意味着在超大规模环境中，你会看到一种特定类型的机架，其中可能包含分离的 CPU 和 GPU 机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.68,0:21:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whereas in enterprise, you might want to see more all-in-one racks uh, going forward.\N而在企业环境中，未来你可能会更倾向于看到更多一体化的机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.36,0:21:09.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'm happy to say this morning, we announced um, the AMD Helion Agentic AI Rack.\N因此，我很高兴今天早上宣布，我们推出了 AMD Helion 代理式 AI 机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.10,0:21:12.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Helion is the cousin to Helios.\NHelion 是 Helios 的表亲。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.20,0:21:19.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh it's really focused on the Agentic AI compute um aspect of it.\N它主要专注于代理式 AI 计算方面的特性。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.21,0:21:26.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh what we're trying to do here is frankly do what is easiest in terms of bringing all of the\N我们在这里真正想做的，是尽可能简化将开放计算基础设施的所有组件整合在一起的过程。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.50,0:21:34.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,pieces of the Open Compute um infrastructure together so that we can get the most efficient uh CPU uh racks.\N这样我们就能获得最高效的 CPU 机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.19,0:21:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that is you can use the you can use a combination of CPUs and GPUs.\N也就是说，你可以使用 CPU 和 GPU 的组合。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.16,0:21:43.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're also um we're also integrating it with a token router.\N此外，我们还集成了一个词元路由器。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.67,0:21:51.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think everyone is talking about how can you most efficiently uh route your um overall AI usage.\N我认为大家都在讨论如何最高效地路由整体 AI 使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.27,0:21:59.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know that within our own IT infrastructure, uh the idea is you don't need the same model for every question.\N我知道在我们自己的 IT 基础设施中，一个核心理念是：并非每个问题都需要同一个模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.13,0:22:01.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't need the same compute for every question.\N并非每个问题都需要同样的计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.66,0:22:08.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want to be able to route uh the right model and the right compute for the right um application.\N你需要能够为合适的应用选择合适的模型和合适的算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.09,0:22:13.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's a key piece of this as well as the overall um open environment.\N这也是整体开放环境中的一个关键部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.64,0:22:22.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, a few of the things about our Helion um Agentic AI Rack, um the nice thing about Helion is we've used uh you know,\N关于我们的 Helion 代理式 AI 机架，有几点值得一提，Helion 的一个优点是，\N我们几乎使用了所有能通过 OCP 规范实现的组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.24,0:22:31.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,practically everything that we could through um OCP's OCP specs uh with the idea of it's a standard 21-inch rack.\N我们采用的是标准的 21 英寸机架，完全遵循 OCP 规范。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.27,0:22:33.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can be liquid or air cooled.\N它支持液冷或风冷。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.73,0:22:42.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is up to 32,000 plus Zen 6 cores, which is 40% more than the other competitive racks.\N最多可提供 32,000 多个 Zen 6 核心，比其他竞争机架多出 40%。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.76,0:22:45.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's the highest compute density in the industry.\N它是业内计算密度最高的机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.67,0:22:55.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,It also can hold up to uh 32 um Instinct MI350P uh GPUs, um as well as a tremendous amount of networking capability.\N它还能容纳多达 32 块 Instinct MI350P GPU，同时具备强大的网络能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.75,0:23:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's all coming together in a um open uh compute uh standard.\N所有这些都汇聚在一个开放的计算标准中。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.36,0:23:08.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look at how we expect these to be used, when you start in a hyperscale configuration,\N当我们考虑这些设备的使用方式时，从超大规模配置开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.92,0:23:15.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,given the density of compute in hyperscale, you would imagine that you would have significant, you know,\N考虑到超大规模环境中的算力密度，你可能会设想在数据中心的某个区域或部署的某个部分，\N集中部署大量 GPU 机架，但你也可以部署代理式 CPU 机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.96,0:23:24.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPU racks in one, you know, portion of the data center or one part of the deployment, but you can have your Agentic CPU racks,\N你可以在同一数据中心中同时拥有 GPU 机架和代理式 CPU 机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.77,0:23:31.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, really sitting side by side and you can mix and match the type of CPU nodes in it.\N你知道，真正地并排摆放，你可以随意搭配不同类型的 CPU 节点。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.45,0:23:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, whether you're looking at personal agents or enterprise agents or technical agents,\N无论是个人智能体、企业智能体还是技术智能体，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.48,0:23:41.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can pick the right compute for the right the right workload.\N你都可以为特定工作负载选择合适的计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.01,0:23:49.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in the enterprise configuration, you can actually add another piece of this, which is, you know, a lot of enterprises are probably,\N在企业配置中，你实际上还可以添加另一部分，比如很多企业可能，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.92,0:23:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, not running the most advanced foundational model, at least when they're running them on prem.\N至少在本地部署时，还没有运行最先进的基础模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.16,0:24:06.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,They could be actually wanting to have the ability to have both CPUs and GPUs in the same rack optimized for their particular workload.\N他们可能确实希望在同一机架中同时拥有 CPU 和 GPU，并针对特定工作负载进行优化。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.44,0:24:10.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, that is what we can do with the Helion rack.\N这正是我们 Helion 机架能够实现的。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.35,0:24:19.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm happy to say that there's been tremendously positive response to the to our Agentic rack.\N很高兴地告诉大家，我们的代理式机架获得了非常积极的反馈。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.60,0:24:20.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you know, two pieces.\N你知道，有两个重点。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.90,0:24:30.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,One is we have a rich ecosystem that are offering the Helion rack starting November 26th and all of this is going to be contributed to OCP.\N一是我们有一个丰富的生态系统，从 11 月 26 日起\N将提供 Helion 机架，所有这些都将贡献给 OCP。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.78,0:24:40.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you know, very excited for that.\N所以，对此我们非常激动。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.68,0:24:46.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so in the final few minutes, I thought I would just give you an update on our silicon.\N好，最后几分钟，我想跟大家更新一下我们的硅基技术进展。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:46.44,0:24:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are always pushing the bleeding edge of silicon, as I said.\N我们始终在推动硅基技术的最前沿，正如我之前所说。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.72,0:24:51.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,In July,\N七月份时，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.53,0:24:59.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,we talked about our Venice portfolio and our our uh We believe these are the the best server portfolio\N我们讨论了我们的Venice系列产品，以及我们认为这是针对大型机架的最佳服务器产品组合，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.98,0:25:05.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,for a gigantic racks because we have the ability uh to really mix and match for the right workload.\N因为我们有能力真正灵活地组合搭配，以满足不同工作负载的需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.59,0:25:12.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we talked about the various flavors of Venice including our workhorse um for gigantic CPU servers,\N我们谈到了Venice系列的各种版本，包括我们用于大型 CPU 服务器的主力型号，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.39,0:25:21.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,the Venice 256 core, our general purpose CPU servers as well as our CPUs for host nodes, the Venice um high frequency.\NVenice 256 核心产品，也包括我们的通用 CPU 服务器，\N以及用于主机节点的Venice高频型号。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.58,0:25:32.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of that is great, but I have uh when I saw you in July, I showed you four pieces of silicon and uh we have some new silicon to show you today.\N所有这些都很出色，但当我七月份见到你时，我向你展示了四块硅芯片，\N而今天我们要向你展示一些全新的硅芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.35,0:25:36.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, let me show you.\N所以，让我来展示一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:36.72,0:25:37.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here we go.\N好，开始了。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.67,0:25:47.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is our new EPYC Verano\N这是我们最新的 EPYC Verano，Verano 基于Venice系列的 CPU 核心。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.89,0:25:52.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,is based on uh the Venice family of CPU cores.\N这款芯片实际上针对的是最低系统功耗进行了优化，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.37,0:25:56.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this guy is actually optimized for the lowest system power,\N这颗芯片实际上针对最低系统功耗做了优化，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.37,0:26:05.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,so it actually has uh six uh CCDs or six CPU core dies um that uh have 32 cores each up to 192 cores.\N所以它实际上有六个 CCD 或六个 CPU 核心芯片，\N每个芯片有 32 个核心，最多可达 192 个核心。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.25,0:26:14.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with that, we've also updated the uh CPU to GPU bandwidth, which makes it um exceptionally good for uh head node solutions as well.\N同时，我们还提升了 CPU 到 GPU 的带宽，这使得它在头节点解决方案方面也表现出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.46,0:26:16.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh Verano looks fantastic.\N所以，Verano看起来非常棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.24,0:26:26.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh there's a lot of excitement about Verano as well as the rest of the Venice family and uh we will be in production in uh the first half of 2027.\NVerano以及整个Venice系列都引发了大量关注，我们将在 2027 年上半年投入生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.80,0:26:31.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, with that, um let me conclude and say, "Look, we love OCP.\N那么，借此机会，让我做个总结，说一句：“我们热爱 OCP。”
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.36,0:26:33.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We love the open ecosystem.\N我们热爱开放生态系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.73,0:26:38.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um open is a foundation for what we care about at AMD.\N开放是我们 AMD 所关注一切的基础。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.11,0:26:40.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it is uh open on every level.\N它在每个层面都是开放的。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.09,0:26:42.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's open on the hardware level.\N硬件层面是开放的。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.16,0:26:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it's open with specs.\N规格也是开放的。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.96,0:26:45.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's working with our partners.\N我们正与合作伙伴紧密协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.38,0:26:50.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's open on the software level working with um all of the software uh vendors to\N软件层面也是开放的，正与所有软件供应商合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.08,0:26:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,ensure that we are uh bringing that together and it's open on the ecosystem side as well.\N确保我们能够把各方整合在一起，同时在生态系统方面也保持开放。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.92,0:27:00.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'm very happy to say a lot of our partners are here at OCP this week.\N所以，我很高兴地告诉大家，我们很多合作伙伴本周都来到了 OCP。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.77,0:27:08.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think it's fantastic all of the work that's coming together and all of the learnings that we will get from bringing um the teams together.\N我认为，所有这些工作的汇聚，以及通过整合团队所获得的诸多经验，都非常棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.07,0:27:15.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, again, I want to say a big thank you to OCP for really bringing together this what I would call collaboration at scale.\N因此，再次感谢 OCP，真正实现了我所说的规模化协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.84,0:27:21.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's an opportunity for each of us to innovate on the things that we're best at and also for each of us\N这为我们每个人提供了机会，专注于我们最擅长的领域进行创新，同时也让我们
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.90,0:27:28.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,to bring together all of the components um across the industry so that we can get solutions to the market uh faster.\N能够整合整个行业中的所有组件，从而更快地将解决方案推向市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.97,0:27:30.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, with that, thank you very much.\N因此，非常感谢大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.91,0:27:34.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have a great OCP.\N祝大家 OCP 顺利。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.76,0:27:36.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Please\N请
